# End-to-end AOTI deployment test: load today's real checkpoint as an AOTInductor .pt2
# in the C++ pair_style and run MD. pair_style cutoff = the model's training cutoff 6.0
# (edges are built within cutsq_global_ = arg^2, pair_mff_torch.cpp:639). cutoff 6.0 ->
# ghost cutoff 7 -> Nghost 512 -> ntotal 762, matching the N baked into core_real762.pt2.
# Atoms are frozen (setforce) so ntotal stays 762 across steps (real forces would move
# them and change the ghost count).
# run 0 = single eval (crashes cleanly if N mismatches); run 100 = stability + timing.
units metal
atom_style atomic
boundary p p p

region box block 0 30 0 30 0 30
create_box 2 box
create_atoms 1 random 150 12345 box
create_atoms 2 random 100 12346 box
mass 1 1.008
mass 2 15.999

neighbor 1.0 bin
neigh_modify every 1 delay 0 check yes

pair_style mff/torch 6.0 cuda
pair_coeff * * /home/ylzhang/lrx/mff_md_work/core_real762.pt2 H O

fix 1 all nve
fix 2 all setforce 0.0 0.0 0.0
thermo 20
thermo_style custom step temp pe etotal
run 0
run 100
